📊 Power BI Project Documentation: E-commerce Sales & Performance Analysis
📌 Executive Summary
This project presents an end-to-end interactive dashboard designed in Power BI using the cleaned sales dataset Ecommerce_Sales_Cleaned_data (1).xlsx. The primary objective is to analyze transaction metrics, revenue distributions across product categories, order status patterns, and customer payment behaviors to enable data-driven operational decisions.

📁 Dataset & Data Architecture
Dataset Overview
Total Records: 1,200 unique orders

Unique Customers: 1,189 customers

Date Range Analyzed: January 2023 – Mid 2025

Primary Key: OrderID

Data Dictionary
Field Name	Data Type	Description
OrderID	String	Unique transaction identifier
Date	Date	Date of transaction
CustomerID	String	Unique identifier for customer
Product	String	Category of hardware/furniture sold
Quantity	Integer	Number of units purchased
UnitPrice	Decimal	Cost per individual unit ($)
ShippingAddress	String	Customer delivery location
PaymentMethod	String	Mode of transaction (Credit Card, Online, Cash, etc.)
OrderStatus	String	Current status (Delivered, Shipped, Pending, Cancelled, Returned)
TrackingNumber	String	Unique shipment tracking code
ItemsInCart	Integer	Total items in cart during session
CouponCode	String	Promo code applied (SAVE10, FREESHIP, etc.)
ReferralSource	String	Acquisition channel (Instagram, Email, Facebook, etc.)
TotalPrice	Decimal	Calculated total revenue ($)
💡 Key Business Metrics & Calculations (DAX Measures)
Code snippet
// Total Revenue
Total Revenue = SUM('Ecommerce_Sales'[TotalPrice])

// Total Orders
Total Orders = DISTINCTCOUNT('Ecommerce_Sales'[OrderID])

// Average Order Value (AOV)
Average Order Value = DIVIDE([Total Revenue], [Total Orders], 0)

// Total Units Sold
Total Quantity Sold = SUM('Ecommerce_Sales'[Quantity])
