2. Revenue by Product Category
Chairs ($195.6K) and Printers ($195.6K) generate the highest revenue share.

Phones ($151.7K) present the lowest relative revenue share despite stable order volume.

3. Operational Order Breakdown
Cancelled & Returned Orders: Combined, cancelled (250) and returned (247) orders account for ~41% of total transactions.

Fulfillment Tracking: 231 delivered, 235 shipped, and 237 pending orders.

4. Payment Channel Distribution
Credit Card ($263.8K) and Online Transfers ($262.4K) drive the highest transaction revenue, though Cash, Gift Cards, and Debit Cards maintain balanced utilization (~20% distribution each).

🛠️ Data Cleaning & Transformations Applied
Formatting & Data Types: Ensured TotalPrice and UnitPrice are strictly formatted to currency decimals; verified datetime formatting on Date.

Calculated Columns Validation: Verified that TotalPrice = Quantity * UnitPrice.

Null & Duplicate Auditing: Cleaned trailing spaces and missing values across shipping address string fields.

🚀 Strategic Recommendations
Fulfillment Optimization: Investigating why ~41% of orders end up cancelled or returned can yield immediate revenue recovery.

Cross-Selling & Promotions: Pair low-margin or lower-selling items like Phones with high-performing essentials like Monitors and Desks.

Payment Gateways: Continue optimizing digital channels (Credit/Online) while retaining flexible payment options due to balanced payment preference.
